stateDiagram-v2
  %% Today's code (the "current" design of AcpApprovals.tla), as a person sees a shared session.
  %% Drawn from TLC's shortest counterexamples for the three rules it breaks.
  [*] --> OpenAlone
  state "Open, only the opener" as OpenAlone
  state "Open, the opener and a follower" as Pair
  state "Turn running" as Running
  state "Question open, the main client holds it" as Asked
  state "Main left, the next client asked again" as Reasked
  state "Main picks allow for this session on a turn it did not start" as Granted
  state "Question decided, turn goes on" as Decided
  state "Nobody open, question denied" as Denied

  OpenAlone --> Pair : a second client opens the session
  OpenAlone --> Running : the opener sends a prompt
  Pair --> Running : the opener sends a prompt
  Running --> Asked : the turn asks for permission
  Asked --> Decided : the main answers once or rejects
  Asked --> Reasked : the main client leaves, another stays
  Asked --> Granted : the main answers allow for this session, and a follower sent the prompt
  Asked --> Denied : the last client leaves
  Reasked --> Decided : the new main answers
  Granted --> Decided : the grant is kept for the session
  Decided --> Running : the turn goes on
  Running --> OpenAlone : the turn ends with one client
  Running --> Pair : the turn ends with two clients

  note right of Asked
    BROKEN: EveryClientGetsQuestion. A follower is open, and the question
    is held by the main only. Shortest path: the opener prompts, a second
    client joins, the turn asks (3 steps from the start).
  end note

  note right of Reasked
    BROKEN: NoReAsk. The main left, and the next client got the question
    again under a new id. Shortest path: a third client joins, the opener
    prompts, the turn asks, the opener leaves (4 steps).
  end note

  note right of Granted
    BROKEN: OnlySenderAlways. The main client, which did not send the prompt,
    decided "allow for this session", and that grant is kept for the whole
    session. Shortest path: a third client joins, that client prompts, the
    turn asks, the main answers always (4 steps).
  end note

  note left of Denied
    Holds: DeniedWhenNoClient. A question is denied once no client is left.
  end note
